#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151846 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class"}] :question/id #uuid "41276052-e364-593e-9557-5d645f169a74" :question/math-academy-id "e-14600" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[5]_{8}$?\n\n1. $-3$\n2. $13$\n3. $3$" :question/worked-solution "The residue class $[5]_{8}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $5$ modulo $8$. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n[5]_{8} &= {x ∈ Z\\begin{vmatrix}x≡5(mod8)} \\\\ = {x ∈ Z \\mid x = 5 + 8k, k ∈ Z} \\\\ = {5 + 8k\\end{vmatrix}k ∈ Z} \\\\\n&= {…, 5 - 2 \\cdot 8, 5 - 8, 5, 5 + 8, 5 + 2 \\cdot 8, …} \\\\\n&= {…,-11,-3, 5, 13, 21, …}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-3$ and $13$ belong to $[5]_{8}$, while $3$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151847 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c1fe7ea-d91e-5440-b756-37a460a18f19" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Residue Classes Containing a Given Element"}] :question/id #uuid "33da67df-113b-58e2-ad3e-a45d1568d75d" :question/math-academy-id "e-14601" :question/problem "Which of the following residue classes modulo $3$ contain the integer $7$?\n\n1. $[4]_3$\n2. $[-1]_3$\n3. $[1]_3$" :question/worked-solution "We have $7 \\in [a]_{3}$ if\n$7 \\equiv a \\quad (\\text{mod}\\:3)$.\n\nLet's now consider each of the given equivalence classes.\n\n- $7 \\in [4]_3$ because $7 \\equiv 4 \\: (\\text{mod}\\:3)$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n- $7 \\not\\in [-1]_3$ because $7 \\not\\equiv -1 \\: (\\text{mod}\\:3)$ $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n- $7 \\in [1]_3$ because $7 \\equiv 1 \\: (\\text{mod}\\:3)$ $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151848 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152099 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6097ae19-85d5-5ca9-892d-889e843b3def" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Residue Classes"}] :question/id #uuid "edf5a7d6-354d-534b-a8d3-5b29f2357a70" :question/math-academy-id "e-14602" :question/problem "If $[a]_n$ denotes the residue class containing all integers congruent to $a$ modulo $n$, then which of the following residue classes is equal to $[13]_3$?\n\n1. $[0]_3$\n2. $[1]_3$\n3. $[2]_3$" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n[a]_{3} = [b]_{3}\n$$\n\nif\n$a \\equiv b \\quad (\\text{mod}\\:3)$.\n\nThe residue class $[13]_{3}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $13$ modulo $3$.\n\nWe can find an alternative representation for this residue class as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n[13]_{3} &= {x ∈ Z\\begin{vmatrix}x≡13(mod3)} \\\\ = {x ∈ Z \\mid x≡4 \\cdot 3 + 1(mod3)} \\\\ = {x ∈ Z \\mid x≡4 \\cdot 0 + 1(mod3)} \\\\ = {x ∈ Z\\end{vmatrix}x≡1(mod3)} \\\\\n&= [1]_{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151850 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152100 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1a842b5-7256-59cd-b33f-d590bc315d84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements"}] :question/id #uuid "e8470a32-e938-5ae5-a732-688a6d62cefd" :question/math-academy-id "e-14604" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. There are $4$ distinct residue classes modulo $8$\n2. $[5]_{3} \\cap [9]_{3} = \\emptyset$\n3. $\\mathbb{Z} = [4]_{3} \\cup [5]_{3} \\cup [9]_{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_n \\cap [b]_n = \\emptyset$ if $a \\not\\equiv b \\: (\\text{mod}\\:n)$\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: $\\mathbb{Z} = [0]_n \\cup [1]_n \\cup \\cdots \\cup [n-1]_n$\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: $\\mathbb{Z}_n = \\big\\{[0]_n,\\, [1]_n,\\, \\ldots,\\, [n-1]_n\\big\\}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. There are exactly $8$ distinct residue classes modulo $8$.\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $5 \\not\\equiv 9 \\: (\\text{mod}3)$, we have that $[5]_3\\cap [9]_3= \\emptyset$.\n- Statement III is true. First, notice the following:\n$[4]_{3}|= [1 + 3 \\cdot 1]_{3} = [1]_{3}; [5]_{3}|= [2 + 3 \\cdot 1]_{3} = [2]_{3}; [9]_{3}|= [0 + 3 \\cdot 3]_{3} = [0]_{3}$\nAs a result, we get\n$[4]_{3}∪[5]_{3}∪[9]_{3}|= [1]_{3}∪[2]_{3}∪[0]_{3}; = [0]_{3}∪[1]_{3}∪[2]_{3}; = Z$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d2f207a-8e99-5520-ab9f-266c8f54465b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to a Residue Class"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e4b3c7f-4b88-526e-97d9-fd8be276ab63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151260} {:answer/id #uuid "f808a749-ed43-5f58-bd9c-ec95f09fb290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151261} {:answer/id #uuid "046aaf12-e7ec-565e-be73-2f99c4b629e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151262} {:answer/id #uuid "3b4af219-d56e-5177-8f5a-66102b140414" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151263} {:answer/id #uuid "4e37192f-fef7-552f-987e-58ce190a880f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151264}] :answer-field/id #uuid "855a304f-7fb2-5dfa-b6f6-6cfee744f199" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151259}] :question/id #uuid "ba3bb1ff-f2f2-5531-a68f-b27801ed7066" :question/math-academy-id "q-78598" :question/problem "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[6]_{9}$?\n\n1. $-12$\n2. $3$\n3. $24$"}]}
